    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nweocig",
      "content": "Kerala has one of the highest per capita incomes and HDI among Indian states. The economy is driven by services, remittances from Non-Resident Keralites (NRK), tourism, agriculture, and industry. The state follows a unique development model — the 'Kerala Model' — characterized by high human development indicators despite relatively moderate income levels."
    },
